ID: Ch7-Intro
TEXT:

#if(v_ch3_kate_badly_hurt == 0) {
"Barry, I would like to have a word with you, in private," Kate tells me, as the four of us are taking a small break near a river.

The water rushes over gray stones, cold and clear, but the chill coming off her has nothing to do with the stream. Ever since our talk about the stat device two hours ago, she has kept her distance, speaking only in clipped monosyllables. The stare she has been leveling at my spine could freeze iron. Whatever knot is tightening in her head, letting it fester will get someone killed.

"Alright," I say. "Lead the way."

She turns on her heel and heads into the trees. I move to follow, but heavy gauntleted fingers clamp down on my shoulder.

"Remember, Barry... Three taps."

Daren's voice is low and dead level. He means the brass transceiver in my coat pocket, the one he passed me last night. Three quick taps against the casing signals danger. He caught the shift in her too.

I give him a nod, and his grip falls away. I track Kate under the canopy, pine needles deadening our steps. We walk in silence for a minute into the thickening brush.

"How far are we going, exactly?" I ask her back, but she gives no answer, boots crunching steadily over dry twigs.

Another minute deeper into the timber, she stops and wheels around. The look in her eyes is the same iron-cold glare she wore after the dragon fight.

"Are you planning to tell me what--"

Frost flares in her right hand. Before the sentence leaves my mouth, an ice dagger materializes at my throat. I recoil, but my spine hits the rough bark of a pine trunk. Kate presses the tapered blade hard against the hollow beneath my jaw. A sharp sting cuts in, and a warm bead of blood trickles down my neck.

"If you make any kind of noise, I will slit your throat here and now. Do you understand?"
}
#if(v_ch3_kate_badly_hurt == 1) {
