The water rushes over gray stones, cold and clear, but the chill coming off her has nothing to do with the stream. Ever since our talk about the stat device two hours ago, she has kept her distance, speaking only in clipped monosyllables. The stare she has been leveling at my spine could freeze iron. Whatever knot is tightening in her head, letting it fester will get someone killed.

