"Do you really expect me to believe--"

She cuts off when she looks at my face. The smirk is gone, and she knows it.

choice("Continue", Ch7-Sister, v_current_scene = Ch7-Sister)


ID: Ch7-Sister
TEXT:

"It happened fifteen years ago," I tell her. "My family and I were living on an isolated farm, where people didn't know anything about banshees and mages. When my sister started gaining magical powers, we were overjoyed. We thought we had a prodigy in the family. Then one night..."

The memory hits like cold water: the smell of copper, the high, frantic laughter that didn't sound human.

"One night, I came home to find the bodies of my parents lying in pools of blood, with my sister standing above them. Only it wasn't my sister anymore. Everything was different about her, even her magical aura. She was raising her hand over my younger brother, when I picked up a pitchfork from the ground and impaled her with it. She had just awakened, which made her vulnerable. If I had arrived even a few minutes later, no one would have walked out of that room alive."

I pause, looking Kate straight in the eye.

"Daren's transceiver lets me signal danger with three taps. I could have done that the second you put your dagger to my throat. I didn't, for the same reason I came into these woods alone with you. I wanted to talk things through and clear the air between us. Now tell me, Kate--do you still think I made all this up just to gain your trust and capture you?"

Kate's hand holding the dagger trembles, and the fierce determination in her eyes slowly breaks. She lowers the blade, her gaze dropping to the moss by her boots.

"No, I don't," she answers, her voice barely a whisper. "I'm... really sorry. For everything..."

choice(""There's no need to apologize."", Ch7-Apologize, v_current_scene = Ch7-Apologize)
choice(""Are we still friends, then?"", Ch7-Friends, v_current_scene = Ch7-Friends)


ID: Ch7-Apologize
TEXT:

"There's no need to apologize."

"Yes, there is!" she flares, her head snapping up. "I almost murdered you in cold blood! Don't you dare brush this off as if it were nothing!"

"Hey, calm down, I'm still alive, aren't I?"

"That's beside the point! I was ready to slit your throat at a moment's notice. And now you're telling me that we should just forget about this and act like nothing happened?!"

"Alright, fair point. I'm not saying it didn't happen. I'm saying we let bygones be bygones and move on."

"Why?! Why are you still willing to trust me after all that's happened? What's wrong with you? Are you completely out of your mind?"

"Of course I am! Surely, you must have realized this when you found out about the true reason I joined the tournament."

She stares at me, completely thrown.

"So..." I hold out my hand to her. "Are we still friends?"

Kate looks at my open palm, struggling to process the words.

"Friends?... How can you even say such a thing after what just happened? Don't you understand that you're putting yourself in danger by travelling with me?"

"So what? How would travelling with you be any more dangerous than having to fight a stillwater and a dragon in the same day? At least if you're coming with us, I'll feel safer, knowing that you're watching my back."

choice("Continue", Ch7-Idiot, v_current_scene = Ch7-Idiot)


ID: Ch7-Friends
TEXT:

"Are we still friends, then?"

"Friends?..." she asks, shocked.

She searches my face, trying to figure out if I'm being serious or not.

"You're insane," she says. "I almost killed you!"

"But you didn't."

"That's beside the point! I was ready to slit your throat at a moment's notice. And now you're talking to me about friendship? What's wrong with you? Are you completely out of your mind?"

"Of course I am! Surely, you must have realized this when you found out about the true reason I joined the tournament."

She looks at me as if she can't believe the words coming out of my mouth.

"Now, are we friends, or not?" I say, holding out my hand to her.

choice("Continue", Ch7-Idiot, v_current_scene = Ch7-Idiot)


ID: Ch7-Idiot
TEXT:

Kate hesitates, looking at my outstretched hand.

"Are you sure about this?" she asks.

"Yes, yes, I'm sure! Now, come on. Shake my hand, already! My arm is going numb."

A faint, tired smile touches her lips. She sniffs and wipes the tears from her eyes with her sleeve.

"You're an idiot," she tells me as she grabs my hand and squeezes it firmly.

"I know," I tell her as we finish our handshake. "We should be going. Daren and Rose must be getting impatient."

"Wait," she says, stepping in front of me. "I still owe you an explanation for all of this. It's the least I can do."

choice(""Does this have anything to do with the Beacon of Hope?"", Ch7-Beacon, v_current_scene = Ch7-Beacon)
choice(""Can you first tell me who these lessathi are, exactly?"", Ch7-Lessathi, v_current_scene = Ch7-Lessathi)


ID: Ch7-Kill
TEXT:

"I didn't call him here to kill you."

"Shut up! I don't believe a word you're saying!"

Frost snaps across my chest, creeping over my shoulders and locking me tight against the pine trunk. Ice encases me from the collar down.

"This ends now," Kate says, pulling her dagger back from my throat to prepare the finishing blow.

I heave against the ice block, but the only part of my body that moves is my head. Daren, where are you?

"This is for Diane, you bastard!" Kate shouts as she swings her ice dagger towards my face.

Her wrist locks two inches from my eyes. Her hand holding the dagger trembles violently. She stares straight into my eyes and strains to force the blade forward, but she can't bring herself to do it. The rage in her face melts away, her eyes watering up. Her grip weakens, and the dagger slips from her fingers, shattering against the ground.

"I'm sorry..." she sobs, tears streaming down her face. "I'm so sorry... For everything..."

"That's enough, Kate," Daren's voice rings out as he steps from behind a tree, sword drawn. "Surrender now, and I won't have to hurt you."

"Daren, wait--" I start to say, but he cuts me off.

"I'm sorry, Barry, but now that it's come to this, I can't just let it slide. She's too dangerous to be left alone. I'm going to purify her."

Kate wipes the tears from her face, her expression hardening back into ice as she turns to Daren.

"Don't sound so disappointed, Daren. We both know that you've been waiting for this moment ever since you first laid eyes on me. And we both know that surrendering is just not in my nature."

"As you wish," Daren says curtly, and rushes towards Kate with sword in hand.

choice("Continue", Ch7-Daren-vs-Kate, v_current_scene = Ch7-Daren-vs-Kate)


