"But why would a dwarf like Hadrik know this credo?" Rose asks, still confused.

"It's because he isn't actually a dwarf. He's a giant shapeshifting as one."

choice("Continue", Ch7-Home-address, v_current_scene = Ch7-Home-address)


ID: Ch7-Home-address
TEXT:

"What?!" Daren asks, utterly shocked.

"That's some really impressive deductive skills there, Barry," Hadrik tells me. "How did you figure it out?"

"Ever since the clearing, your aura showed an active shapeshift. But shapeshifting magic only alters scale or form—it can't manufacture a personal disguise. Then I remembered your fifty-foot form from earlier. Magic can't expand a mortal tenfold, but a giant can compress into a dwarf. The colossus was your natural body."

Hadrik laughs again, clapping his thighs.

"Well, you found out my secret," he says. "What are you going to do now? Will you report me to the organizers so that they can kick me out of the tournament? Are you going to use this information to blackmail me into helping you with the objectives?"

"What? No, don't be ridiculous. If I did that, what stops you from reporting me for entering as an ordinary human? The organizers barely screened entrants anyway. Why would they care about an unregistered giant?"

"Fair point!" Hadrik grins. "Well, that's enough questions for now. Any more and you'll have my home address! Hahahahaha!"

As we push deeper into the forest, glowing yellow orbs begin drifting between the tree trunks, bobbing in lazy orbits.

"What are these?" I ask, pointing to a drifting sphere of light. "Overgrown fireflies?"

"Oh..." Rose gasps, freezing in her tracks. "Oh no... This is bad. We need to leave right now."

"Why? What's wrong?"

"Those aren't fireflies. They are spirits of the forest. We've crossed into the sacred woods by mistake. We aren't permitted here!"

choice(""What are spirits of the forest?"", Ch7-Spirits, v_current_scene = Ch7-Spirits)
choice(""What are sacred woods?"", Ch7-Sacred, v_current_scene = Ch7-Sacred)
choice(""Not allowed by whom?"", Ch7-Allowed, v_current_scene = Ch7-Allowed)


ID: Ch7-Spirits
TEXT:

"What are spirits of the forest?"

"They are guardians," Rose whispers urgently. "Sworn to protect the animals and the groves from harm."

"And who decided we aren't permitted passage?"

"The great golden fox. Please, we have to turn back before it's too late--"

"Kate?..." a woman's voice calls out from behind a thick oak. "Kate, is that you?"

A woman steps into the dim light. She has a lean, muscular build, striking blue eyes, and short blond hair standing on end from residual static. She wears fitted leather trousers and a gray sleeveless tunic, her age matching Kate's. A jagged burn scar wraps around her left forearm.

"Diane!" Kate cries, rushing forward. "I can't believe it's really you... I've been looking for you for so long--"

"You IDIOT!" Diane snaps, cutting her off with a sharp glare. "Why did you come back? You aren't supposed to be here!"

"Diane, listen to me, I came back here to save you... I came back here to take you away from this place."

"I don't need saving!" Diane pulls her collar down, showing bare skin where the suppressing band once rested. "I am working with them of my own free will."

"What?... But, why? I don't understand..."

"It doesn't matter! What matters is that you need to get out of here. Quick! Before the ancients come back. And stop looking for me! Please..."

"No!" Kate shouts. "I'm not leaving here without you!"

"Yes, you are," Diane says, her eyes glowing vibrant blue as crackling arcs of lightning wrap around her arms.

"Kate, we should back off," I tell her, the hair on my arms standing straight from the static charge saturating the air.

"No!" Kate says. "If she doesn't plan to see reason until I beat some sense into her stupid head, then I'll--"

A blinding arc of lightning detonates in our midst. The shockwave hits like a physical hammer, violently arcing through every nerve and slamming us simultaneously to the ground. My muscles seize, but my half-lessathi resistance keeps the darkness at bay while the others lie motionless.

choice("Continue", Ch7-Ending, v_current_scene = Ch7-Ending)


ID: Ch7-Sacred
TEXT:

"What are sacred woods?"

"Sanctuaries where only wildlife is permitted to dwell."

"Who enforces the rule?"

"The great golden fox. Please, we have to turn back before it's too late--"

