choice("Continue", Ch7-Ending, v_current_scene = Ch7-Ending)


ID: Ch7-Ending
TEXT:

Two figures in dark blue robes emerge from the shadows behind Diane, deep hoods hiding their features.

"What is this?" the one on the right asks, scanning the fallen. "More intruders?"

"Look," the left one says. "The dwarf she spared this afternoon. He returned with reinforcements."

He glares at Diane.

"Well? Finish them. Or do you intend to wait until they bring an army?"

"No," Diane says, voice cold and steady. "I won't kill them."

"Useless," the right-hand man snorts, stepping forward with drawn steel. "Stand aside. I'll do it."

"Touch one of them," Diane says, crackling blue sparks leaping between her fingers, "and I murder you where you stand."

"You dare threaten your masters, wench?"

"Enough, Zenir," the left-hand man says, catching his partner's arm. "You know we cannot best her in combat. Our position is compromised. Prepare the camp for relocation."

"Fine," Zenir spits, sheathing his blade. "Lady Meridith will hear of your insubordination."

"Count on it," Diane replies with a defiant smirk.

The two ancients turn and vanish into the brush. Once the trees swallow them, Diane looks down at the five of us, her gaze landing on me.

"Still awake?" she murmurs, stepping closer. "Strange... that voltage drops any human cold. How are you conscious?"

She leans down, her eyes widening as she reads my aura, followed by a faint, knowing smile.

"I see. You are a lessathi. Kate must place immense trust in you to travel together."

"Wait," I manage to gasp, my chest burning. "Why are you--"

"Take good care of her, will you?" Diane says, placing a soft finger against my forehead. "I'm counting on you to keep her safe."

A fresh surge of electricity discharges through my skull. The last thing I see is her sad, quiet smile as my vision collapses into black.

